{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ page_title }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <h1 class="display-4 mb-4" style="color: #155263;">{{ page_title }}</h1>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-8">
            <p class="lead">
                Welcome to our simple <strong>Symfony Gallery application</strong>, built as an portfolio project.
                My goal is to demonstrate key techniques used in modern Symfony applications,
                specifically: <strong>modular Twig</strong>, <strong>Dependency Injection (DI)</strong>, and <strong>Symfony Forms</strong>.
            </p>

            <h2 class="mt-5" style="color: #1e758d;">Our Architecture</h2>
            <p>
                The application relies on <strong>Bootstrap 5</strong> for full responsiveness and utilizes the <strong>Controller-View</strong> pattern (MVC).
            </p>
            <ul class="list-unstyled">
                <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success" style="color: #ffbb09;"></i> <strong>Controllers:</strong> Use of `#[Route]` attributes and service injection (e.g., `SluggerInterface`).</li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success" style="color: #ffbb09;"></i> <strong>Views:</strong> Architecture with inheritance (`base.html.twig`) and composition (`_navbar.html.twig`).</li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success" style="color: #ffbb09;"></i> <strong>Forms:</strong> Handling single data (gallery name) and file collections (pictures) with validation.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card shadow-sm border-0" style="background-color: #ffd76f;">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h5 class="card-title" style="color: #0c2f39;">Symfony Core</h5>
                    <p class="card-text small">7.4.0</p>
                    <h5 class="card-title" style="color: #0c2f39;">Front-end</h5>
                    <p class="card-text small">Framework: Bootstrap 5</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}